{
  "metadata": {
    "source": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
    "last_verified": "2026-06-28",
    "currency": "USD",
    "schema_version": "1",
    "conventions": {
      "price_entry_shape": {
        "price": "number (USD)",
        "unit": "always 'USD'",
        "billing_unit": "per_1M_tokens",
        "dimension": "input | input_cache_hit | output"
      },
      "lookup_key_pattern": "{canonical_model_id}#{tier}#{dimension}",
      "tier_values": "standard | batch | long_context_standard | long_context_batch",
      "resolution_flow": "any_string -> model_string_index -> canonical_id -> lookup key",
      "cache_note": "Cached input (automatic prompt caching) billed at input_cache_hit price; non-cached input at input price. Reasoning/'pro' models do not expose a cached-input rate — cached tokens fall back to the full input price in PriceManager.",
      "batch_note": "Batch API (async) is a uniform 50% discount on input, cached input, and output. Batch entries are derived as standard x 0.5.",
      "long_context_note": "long_context_standard / long_context_batch apply when total prompt tokens > 272,000 (the long_context threshold); PriceManager switches to these keys automatically when the model publishes them (see gpt_5_6_coverage_note). Below the threshold, standard / batch apply. Published for gpt-5.4-pro and every model at or above it in the GPT-5.x line (gpt-5.4-pro, gpt-5.4, gpt-5.5-pro, gpt-5.5, gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-luna); earlier/smaller models (gpt-5.4-mini, gpt-5.4-nano, gpt-5.3-codex, chatgpt-latest, gpt-5.6-cyber) do not publish a long-context rate.",
      "gpt_5_5_pro_batch_note": "Source page returned an anomalous batch rate for gpt-5.5-pro (higher than standard); corrected to the standard 50% discount, matching its sibling gpt-5.4-pro.",
      "coverage_note": "Only the GPT-5.x generation (plus chatgpt-latest and gpt-5.3-codex) is listed on the developer pricing page. Earlier families (gpt-4.1, gpt-4o, o3, o4-mini) were not present and are intentionally omitted.",
      "gpt_5_6_coverage_note": "gpt-5.6-sol/terra/luna source data also publishes a flex tier, a fast_mode tier, and a cache_writes dimension. flex is numerically identical to batch for every gpt-5.6 model, so omitting it loses no information; fast_mode and cache_writes have no equivalent tier/dimension in this schema and are genuinely dropped. gpt-5.6-cyber's source only publishes a standard short_context tier (no batch, no long_context). long_context_batch entries for gpt-5.4-pro/gpt-5.4/gpt-5.5-pro/gpt-5.5 are derived as long_context_standard x 0.5 (source did not publish batch or long_context_batch rates directly for these models, but every other batch entry in this file matches this ratio exactly)."
    }
  },
